# MCUHome Matter framework component (docs/design/component-model.md §2,
# "core" kind): wires upstream CHIP (connectedhomeip) into the MCUHome
# runtime — PSA crypto, Thread/OpenThread defaults, dynamic-endpoint
# support. C sources land in Block A4; this only wires the Kconfig tree.

menuconfig MCUHOME_MATTER
	bool "MCUHome Matter framework"
	depends on CHIP
	depends on MCUHOME
	# CHIP's own Kconfig (modules/lib/connectedhomeip/config/zephyr/Kconfig)
	# does `imply NEWLIB_LIBC_NANO` — an *imply*, not a hard `select`, and
	# LIBC_IMPLEMENTATION is a `choice`: choice symbols can never be
	# `select`ed, by upstream or by us, only steered via `default`/prompt.
	# On nRF52840 the newlib-nano default heap setup dies pre-main
	# (bisected 2026-08-03), before any of our code — or even the rest of
	# Kconfig — gets a chance to react. There is no runtime hook left to
	# catch this once it happens. Depending on PICOLIBC here instead turns
	# a silent pre-main crash on the bench into a loud configure-time
	# dependency error (missing CONFIG_PICOLIBC=y) at `west build` time.
	depends on PICOLIBC
	# CHIP's UDP endpoints need IPv6 packet info (recvmsg ancillary data) to
	# answer from the correct source address; without this option the
	# IPV6_RECVPKTINFO setsockopt fails (errno 109) and PASE handshakes die
	# silently — the commissioner sees "address unreachable".
	select NET_CONTEXT_RECV_PKTINFO
	# SLAAC is off in vanilla Zephyr (NCS turns it on): without it the device
	# never gets an address from the border router's OMR prefix, and the SRP
	# server rejects the host registration ("internal server error") — the
	# node is then invisible to Matter on-network discovery.
	select OPENTHREAD_SLAAC if NET_L2_OPENTHREAD
	help
	  Enables the MCUHome Matter (CHIP) integration: PSA crypto wiring,
	  Thread/OpenThread defaults and the dynamic-endpoint runtime that the
	  builder drives from generated device tables. See
	  docs/design/matter-zephyr-integration.md for the findings behind
	  the defaults this symbol pulls in.

if MCUHOME_MATTER

config MCUHOME_MATTER_PSA_WANTS
	bool
	default y if MBEDTLS
	# The PSA_WANT_* symbols are promptless while MBEDTLS_PROMPTLESS is
	# active — plain prj.conf assignments are silently dropped. An app
	# Kconfig `select` is the supported way to force them on. CHIP needs
	# HKDF (SPAKE2+ key derivation — missing it kills PASE with a silent
	# INTERNAL after the point math), ECDH (CASE), SHA-1 (certificates)
	# and PBKDF2 (PASE prover side).
	select PSA_WANT_ALG_HKDF
	select PSA_WANT_ALG_ECDH
	select PSA_WANT_ALG_SHA_1
	select PSA_WANT_ALG_PBKDF2_HMAC
	select PSA_WANT_KEY_TYPE_DERIVE
	select PSA_WANT_KEY_TYPE_HMAC

choice MCUHOME_MATTER_THREAD_ROLE
	prompt "Thread device role"
	depends on NET_L2_OPENTHREAD
	default MCUHOME_MATTER_THREAD_ROUTER
	help
	  CHIP ThreadStackManager device role, set at startup via
	  ConnectivityManager::SetThreadDeviceType(). Sleepy End Device (SED)
	  support is not offered here yet — it lands with the power-management
	  phase (ICD configuration, poll period, Matter LIT/SIT semantics).

config MCUHOME_MATTER_THREAD_ROUTER
	bool "Router (FTD)"
	help
	  Full Thread Device: participates in mesh routing, radio always on.
	  Correct choice for mains-powered nodes.

config MCUHOME_MATTER_THREAD_MED
	bool "Minimal End Device (MED)"
	help
	  Minimal End Device: does not route for other devices, but (unlike a
	  Sleepy End Device) keeps its radio on. Use this for battery-powered
	  nodes until SED support lands.

endchoice

endif # MCUHOME_MATTER
